fact WorkItem(id: "WI-617", description: some(value: "Typer robustness (follow-up to WI-614, /code-review finding): spec_has_any_providers (kb/typing.rs:8828) compares view_base_sym == spec_sort with RAW == instead of canonical same_symbol/canonical_sort_sym — inconsistent with its sibling impl_sorts_providing_spec (typing.rs:8758, which canonicalizes). A sort interns under multiple Symbol ids (bare vs qualified); if a provider fact's spec base interns differently from the queried spec symbol, == reads false -> spec_has_any_providers returns false -> carrier_is_abstract_spec returns false -> the abstract-spec-carrier dispatch gates (WI-598/601/608/609/614) spuriously SKIP, so a legitimately-abstract spec value (e.g. a FiniteCollection map/filter result) regresses to a loud 'no such member (dot dispatch)' / missing-dispatch error. Completeness/robustness gap (loud failure, never a wrong result); low-confidence it mis-fires on the current stdlib (finiteness suite is green) but it is load-bearing for the whole carrier_is_abstract_spec gate. FIX: canonicalize both sides (kb.canonical_sort_sym(view_base_sym) == kb.canonical_sort_sym(spec_sort)), matching impl_sorts_providing_spec. ACCEPTANCE: cargo-test; ideally a regression test with a provider fact whose spec base interns under a non-canonical symbol."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-614"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-02T19:49:35Z"))

fact Tag(workitem: "WI-617", name: "finiteness")
